{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQ15xKZYduEq2VUQhaoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FLesKvj7iGxszutGJin4cT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\nL=open(p).read().split('\\n')\ni=[k for k,l in enumerate(L) if l.startswith('8. **Open or update a draft PR**')][0]\nL[i]+=\" **PR creation failure and recovery (#435).** `CreatePR` is retried when the failure is transient (`github.IsTransient`: 5xx, rate limit, network timeout), up to 4 attempts with 2 s, 5 s and 15 s waits; before each retry the loop looks for a PR on the head, in case the failed create reached GitHub. Under dry-run it logs `worker.pr_retry` and does not retry. When the create still fails after this job pushed the branch, the job records the branch, head, PR title and body, summary and worker result in the nullable `jobs.pending_pr` column (migration 0009; older rows read as none) and ends `executor:failed` with the cause `pr_create_failed` (not transient, not auto-retried) and one comment naming the branch and short head: only the PR is missing. When a human removes `executor:failed`, the next worker job looks at the newest earlier worker job of the issue and role; if it has a record, the branch tip is its recorded head (or only adds files under `.ard/`, which is the failed job's own close-out commit) and no open PR exists for the branch, the loop opens the PR from the record and closes the job done with no agent run and no test run (`WorkerResult.Reopened`; close-out reads no role file and takes the recorded summary). Otherwise, or if the lookup fails, the full worker runs as before. The built-in engineer prompt also tells the agent to answer `done` with the original summary when the branch already holds the complete change and no PR exists.\"\nopen(p,'w').write('\\n'.join(L))\np='internal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''- Write .ard/N/worker-engineer.md, your report. Write it whole, even if an\n  earlier run left one.\n''','''- When the branch already holds a complete implementation of the plan\n  (its own earlier work) and no pull request exists, answer done with the\n  original summary of that work, not needs-human.\n- Write .ard/N/worker-engineer.md, your report. Write it whole, even if an\n  earlier run left one.\n''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat internal/roles; cat >> internal/state/store_test.go <<'EOF'\n\nfunc TestPendingPR(t *testing.T) {\n\tctx := tctx(t)\n\ts := newStore(t)\n\tj, err := s.CreateJob(ctx, NewJob{Stage: \"worker\", Role: \"eng\", Issue: 7})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif got, _ := s.Job(ctx, j.ID); got.PendingPR != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"new job pending = %s, want none\", got.PendingPR)\n\t}\n\tif err := s.SetPendingPR(ctx, j.ID, PendingPR{Branch: \"b\"}); err == nil {\n\t\tt.Error(\"a record with no head was accepted\")\n\t}\n\twant := PendingPR{Branch: \"worker/eng-7-x\", Head: \"abc\", Title: \"t\", Body: \"b\", Summary: \"s\", Result: []byte(`{\"PR\":0}`)}\n\tif err := s.SetPendingPR(ctx, j.ID, want); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\t// The record is read only from an ended job other than the caller's.\n\tif _, _, ok, err := s.LatestPendingPR(ctx, 7, \"eng\", \"\"); err != nil || ok {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"running job: ok=%v err=%v\", ok, err)\n\t}\n\tif err := s.Fail(ctx, j.ID, \"pr_create_failed\", time.Time{}); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\t_, got, ok, err := s.LatestPendingPR(ctx, 7, \"eng\", \"other\")\n\tif err != nil || !ok || got.Head != \"abc\" || got.Branch != want.Branch || string(got.Result) != `{\"PR\":0}` {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pending = %+v ok=%v err=%v\", got, ok, err)\n\t}\n\tif _, _, ok, _ := s.LatestPendingPR(ctx, 7, \"eng\", j.ID); ok {\n\t\tt.Error(\"the caller's own job was returned\")\n\t}\n\t// A newer job without a record supersedes it.\n\ts2, err := s.CreateJob(ctx, NewJob{Stage: \"worker\", Role: \"eng\", Issue: 7})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif err := s.Fail(ctx, s2.ID, \"x\", time.Time{}); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif _, _, ok, _ := s.LatestPendingPR(ctx, 7, \"eng\", \"other\"); ok {\n\t\tt.Error(\"a superseded record was returned\")\n\t}\n}\nEOF\ngofmt -l internal; go test ./internal/state/ -run PendingPR 2>&1 | tail -15"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1967,"cache_read_input_tokens":93048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1967},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f53e436-51a7-4416-9cdc-1117f8238899","uuid":"6b55df92-94b1-4331-adde-d02ca2ff60d9","timestamp":"2026-11-25T16:59:18.744Z","request_id":"req_011ChQ15xAtJ38vWj31FZzas"}
