{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQ1LRfzKqKPtj2Mozp3x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016f27iRRr3pb3pJexZPEEwB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/work/.ard/435/worker-engineer.md","content":"---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nWhen a worker pushes its branch but GitHub will not open the pull request, the loop now retries the create with backoff, and on final failure records the close-out so a later label removal opens the PR without running the agent.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/worker/prretry.go` (new): `createWithRetry` (4 attempts, 2s/5s/15s backoff, transient errors only via `github.IsTransient`, looks for an existing PR on the head before each retry, no retry under dry-run), `failCreate` and `reopenPR`. The reopen path runs before the agent step. It needs a record from the newest earlier worker job for the issue, a branch tip equal to the recorded head (or only adding files under `.ard/`, the failed job's own close-out commit) and no open PR. Otherwise the full run happens.\n- `internal/worker/run.go`, `loop.go`: `openPR` uses the retry. After a push, a failed create ends with the new cause `pr_create_failed` and stores the record. Without a push it keeps `no_process`. New `Deps.Sleep` and two `Store` methods.\n- `internal/closeout`: new `CausePRCreateFailed` (failed plan, not transient, no retry). `WorkerResult.Reopened` and `Summary` let `Prepare` close a job done with no role file or agent worktree.\n- `internal/state`: migration 0009 adds a nullable `pending_pr` column, so old rows are unaffected. Also `PendingPR`, `SetPendingPR` and `LatestPendingPR`. The schema golden and the schema-version assertion are updated.\n- `internal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt`: rule to answer `done` when the branch already holds the complete change and no PR exists. `docs/proposal.md`: worker step 8 describes the recovery.\n\n## Testing\n`make lint test` passes. New tests use the GitHub fake: retry then open (no second agent step, no `executor:failed`), non-transient error not retried, always-fails records `pr_create_failed` with the branch and head, reopen without an agent, reopen tolerating the close-out `.ard/` commit, branch moved falls back to the full run, existing PR falls back with no duplicate, dry-run does not sleep or retry, sleep stops on cancel, no-push failure keeps `no_process`. Closeout tests cover the reopened result and the `pr_create_failed` plan; a state test covers the record and its supersession. An earlier run of the state tests failed on the schema version and golden file; both were updated.\n\n## Open issues\n- `.ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt` (protected) is not changed; a maintainer must sync the new prompt rule there by hand.\n- Dry-run never reopens a PR from a record; it only logs.\n- A cancelled context during backoff leaves the job running for the Reaper rather than finishing it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":462,"cache_read_input_tokens":99299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":462},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f53e436-51a7-4416-9cdc-1117f8238899","uuid":"55dfa1bb-5f51-44d5-81f3-511abecd584c","timestamp":"2026-11-25T17:02:32.043Z","request_id":"req_011ChQ1LRWZuoCfNJDVfpMHG"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016f27iRRr3pb3pJexZPEEwB","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /work/.ard/435/worker-engineer.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f53e436-51a7-4416-9cdc-1117f8238899","uuid":"8ae6abb9-8f91-4b5d-a743-5b4d7c72d95e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T17:02:32.068Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/work/.ard/435/worker-engineer.md","content":"---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nWhen a worker pushes its branch but GitHub will not open the pull request, the loop now retries the create with backoff, and on final failure records the close-out so a later label removal opens the PR without running the agent.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/worker/prretry.go` (new): `createWithRetry` (4 attempts, 2s/5s/15s backoff, transient errors only via `github.IsTransient`, looks for an existing PR on the head before each retry, no retry under dry-run), `failCreate` and `reopenPR`. The reopen path runs before the agent step. It needs a record from the newest earlier worker job for the issue, a branch tip equal to the recorded head (or only adding files under `.ard/`, the failed job's own close-out commit) and no open PR. Otherwise the full run happens.\n- `internal/worker/run.go`, `loop.go`: `openPR` uses the retry. After a push, a failed create ends with the new cause `pr_create_failed` and stores the record. Without a push it keeps `no_process`. New `Deps.Sleep` and two `Store` methods.\n- `internal/closeout`: new `CausePRCreateFailed` (failed plan, not transient, no retry). `WorkerResult.Reopened` and `Summary` let `Prepare` close a job done with no role file or agent worktree.\n- `internal/state`: migration 0009 adds a nullable `pending_pr` column, so old rows are unaffected. Also `PendingPR`, `SetPendingPR` and `LatestPendingPR`. The schema golden and the schema-version assertion are updated.\n- `internal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt`: rule to answer `done` when the branch already holds the complete change and no PR exists. `docs/proposal.md`: worker step 8 describes the recovery.\n\n## Testing\n`make lint test` passes. New tests use the GitHub fake: retry then open (no second agent step, no `executor:failed`), non-transient error not retried, always-fails records `pr_create_failed` with the branch and head, reopen without an agent, reopen tolerating the close-out `.ard/` commit, branch moved falls back to the full run, existing PR falls back with no duplicate, dry-run does not sleep or retry, sleep stops on cancel, no-push failure keeps `no_process`. Closeout tests cover the reopened result and the `pr_create_failed` plan; a state test covers the record and its supersession. An earlier run of the state tests failed on the schema version and golden file; both were updated.\n\n## Open issues\n- `.ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt` (protected) is not changed; a maintainer must sync the new prompt rule there by hand.\n- Dry-run never reopens a PR from a record; it only logs.\n- A cancelled context during backoff leaves the job running for the Reaper rather than finishing it.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016f27iRRr3pb3pJexZPEEwB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQ1M2kdmbMHeSo7gfnJK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The worker now retries opening the PR when `CreatePR` fails after a push, and a later re-run opens it from the recorded close-out without running the agent. `make lint test` passes.\n\n- **Retry:** transient errors (5xx, rate limit, network timeout) are retried up to four attempts, with waits of 2s, 5s and 15s. Before each retry the loop looks for an existing PR on the branch, in case the failed create actually landed. Under dry-run it only logs.\n- **Final failure:** if the create still fails after this job pushed, the job records the branch, head, title, body and result. It ends `executor:failed` with the new cause `pr_create_failed`, and the comment names the pushed branch and head. If nothing was pushed, the cause stays `no_process`.\n- **Re-run without the agent:** when the label is removed, the next job looks at the newest earlier worker job for that issue. If the branch tip still equals the recorded head and no PR exists, it opens the PR with no agent or test run. Otherwise the full worker runs as before. The new tests cover the moved-branch and existing-PR fallbacks.\n- **Close-out commit:** the failed job's close-out pushes a log commit under `.ard/` on top of the recorded head. The tip check therefore counts a tip that only added `.ard/` files as unchanged.\n- **Store and docs:** a nullable `pending_pr` column (migration 0009) holds the record, so existing rows are unaffected. I updated the schema golden and the schema-version assertion. The engineer prompt template and `docs/proposal.md` step 8 are updated too.\n\nOpen points:\n- A maintainer must sync the prompt rule into `.ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt` by hand, since that path is protected.\n- If the context is cancelled during a backoff, the job stays running for the Reaper rather than finishing.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/435/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":99761,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1222},"output_tokens":633,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f53e436-51a7-4416-9cdc-1117f8238899","uuid":"7b84173f-9fd5-45b4-baa1-760efe965667","timestamp":"2026-11-25T17:02:36.552Z","request_id":"req_011ChQ1M2bxMb28mFWZKjGTt"}
